infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The worker class decides what one worker is
  desc Sync (left): one request per process; uvicorn (right): an event loop with hundreds in flight
  compares
    - label Sync worker
      children
        - label 1 request per process
          desc Concurrency equals the worker count
        - label Blocking drivers are fine
          desc Or run them on thread executors
        - label Slow upstream stalls it
          desc One call holds the whole process
        - label 2*cores+1 heuristic
          desc Sync-era rule of thumb for mixed I/O
    - label Uvicorn worker
      children
        - label Hundreds in flight
          desc One event loop multiplexes the sockets
        - label Everything must await
          desc A stray sync call freezes the loop
        - label 1-2x cores
          desc Extra workers add cores, not concurrency
        - label Wider blast radius
          desc A kill drops every live coroutine
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
